<title>ZIMBABWE: Barclays lifts yr shr, div surges.</title>
<headline>Barclays lifts yr shr, div surges.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>		    (million Z$ unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		130.5	vs     79.9</p>
<p>    Final div (cts)	 40.0	vs     25.0</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		 318.33	vs     191.77</p>
<p>    Tax		     132.13	vs     78.05</p>
<p>    After-tax	     186.20	vs     113.72</p>
<p>Full name: Barclays Bank of Zimbabwe Ltd</p>
<p>Note - The company said that the country would reap the benefits of good rains this year. It said that inflation was set to continue falling, economic output was rising and that these factors should result in lower interest rates that will generate sustained growth throughout 1997.</p>
<p>Barclays said that it had the infrastructure and capacity to play a leading role in the economic development of the country. It said that it was confident that another year of significant contribution and excellent results lay ahead.</p>
<p>-- Harare newsroom +263-4 72 52 28/9</p>
</text>
